    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`import sglang` takes several seconds. `srt/utils/common.py` imported `video_decoder` at module load, which transitively pulls in `torchcodec` — a cost paid on every `import sglang`, even for text-only workloads.\n\n## Change\n\nMove the `video_decoder` import from module level into the functions that use it: `load_audio`, `load_video`, `encode_video`.\n\n## Result\n\nMeasured with `python -X importtime`, A/B alternating in the same container:\n\n- `import sglang`: 7.36s -> 7.20s (-164ms, ~2.2%)\n- `torchcodec` no longer appears on the `import sglang` path\n\nAudio/video decoding still works: `_BACKEND` resolves to `torchcodec` and the decoders load on first use.\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38022591512](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38022591512)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38022591380](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38022591380)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38022591576](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38022591576)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
